Hi!

I have check your code and you are right, the memory allocated is very high (in my case the memory is almost complete with 15 gb (I have 16gb of RAM in my laptop) for the 20000 observations. It is obvious because you are estimating one coefficient for each observation.
However, if you don't specify the knots in the gam function (gam(y~s(E,N,bs='ts'),data=dat,fit=FALSE)) the memory allocated is reduced notably for the same set of 20000 observations (from 6gb to 10gb).

I don't remember exactly how internally works the library 'mgcv' to select the optimum number of knots so you should check the differences for both options (for example, the error between your first model (knots = 60) and your second model (without specify the knots in the gam function).

Cheers

